course: dictionary
lesson: 1518
title: The centime
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A centime is a small coin. It is one hundredth of a franc, so 100 centimes make one franc. The sentence «a euro cent is called un centime» shows that French people use the word centime for a euro cent too. Think of it as the French word for a penny or a cent.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Centimes are small amounts of money, and «cent» means a hundred, so the word comes from the idea of a hundredth. If 100 centimes make one franc, then 50 centimes must be half a franc. Try "penny" or "cent" in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Centimes are not just old money. Switzerland still uses them as one hundredth of a Swiss franc, and some African countries also use them. When you meet a word from another country, context helps, and a dictionary settles what you are not sure of.
fact: A centime is one hundredth of a franc.
fact: 100 centimes make one franc.
fact: «Centime» is said «sahn-TEEM» in French, and «cent» is said «sahn».
fact: In everyday French, «un centime» can mean a euro cent.
fact: Centimes are still used in Switzerland and some African countries.
exercise: In French, what is a «centime»? | A type of cheese | *A small coin, worth one hundredth of a franc | A large banknote used for big shopping | A French word for a bus ticket
exercise: If 100 centimes make one franc, how many centimes make half a franc? | 100 centimes | *50 centimes | 200 centimes | 25 centimes
exercise: Which place still uses centimes, according to the entry? | Japan | Germany | Brazil | *Switzerland, as one hundredth of a Swiss franc
test: In everyday French speech, what does «un centime» mean? | A French franc note | *A euro cent | A kind of bread | A whole euro
test: «Cent» means a hundred. Why does a centime fit that idea? | *Because it is a hundredth of a franc | Because it is the biggest coin | Because it is a hundred francs | Because it is always made of gold
exam: Maths: 100 centimes make one franc. How many centimes make a quarter of a franc? | *25 | 75 | 50 | 10
